    "OverallSummary": "The case involves ACP Securities, LLC failing to disclose on its Form CRS that one of its associated persons had disciplinary history from July 2021 to January 2024. This is not a Care Obligation violation but rather a disclosure violation. The case specifically cites violations of Section 17(a)(1) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934, Exchange Act Rule 17a-14, and FINRA Rule 2010. Form CRS requires firms to disclose whether they or their financial professionals have legal or disciplinary history. Despite having an associated person with reportable disciplinary history (who used a non-firm-approved communications platform to communicate with a customer), ACP Securities repeatedly filed Form CRS documents that failed to acknowledge this disciplinary history. The firm finally corrected this on January 4, 2024. For this willful violation, the firm was censured and fined $20,000. No specific customers were identified as being directly harmed, nor were financial losses documented, as this was primarily a regulatory disclosure violation affecting retail investors generally rather than specific individuals."
